// A callee writes its argument to a global, which the caller reads after the call and passes
// to a sink. The query crosses the call to `put` by its effect on the global without entering
// `put`. The sink is on `snk`'s formal, so it is anchored at the call to `snk` and the flow has
// a step there too.
var g;

def put(v) {
start:
  g.deref = v;
  return;
}

def snk(c) {
start:
  sink(c, Secret);
  return;
}

def main() {
start:
  x = source(Secret);
  put(x);
  y = g.deref;
  snk(y);
  return;
}
